      "page_title": "Enums Are Sum Types",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Sum, Not Int Alias",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`enum` = value is exactly one of N variants",
            "Algebraic sum type, not a C integer alias",
            "Struct = product: A AND B, all fields at once",
            "Enum = sum: A OR B, one variant at a time"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "struct (product)",
                "lines": [
                  "x AND y",
                  "all fields live",
                  "size = sum of parts"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "enum (sum)",
                "lines": [
                  "Circle OR Rect",
                  "one payload live",
                  "size = largest part"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Variant Kinds"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "enum Direction { North, South, East, West }",
            "enum Shape { Circle(f64), Rect(f64,f64) }",
            "enum Event { Click { x: i32, y: i32 },",
            "    KeyPress(char), Close } // mixes all 3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Unit variants carry no data at all",
            "Tuple variants carry positional data",
            "Struct variants carry named fields",
            "One declaration may mix all three kinds"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Namespacing",
          "items": [
            "Write `Direction::North`, never bare `North`",
            "`use Direction::*;` pulls variants into scope",
            "Variants are not free-floating constants"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Variants Are Functions"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "// Some has type fn(T) -> Option<T>",
            "let xs: Vec<Option<i32>> =",
            "    v.into_iter().map(Some).collect();"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Discriminants And Casts"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "enum Status { Ok = 200, NotFound = 404 }",
            "let c = Status::NotFound as i32; // 404",
            "// explicit values: fieldless enums only"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Fieldless enum casts to int with `as`",
            "Int back to enum needs `TryFrom` or a match",
            "No implicit reverse: most ints are invalid"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Traits On Enums",
          "items": [
            "`#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]`",
            "Derive works only if every payload does too",
            "`impl Direction { fn opposite(self) -> Self }`",
            "Inherent + trait impls, same as structs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Recursive And Generic"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "enum List { Cons(i32, Box<List>), Nil }",
            "// no Box => infinite size, rejected",
            "enum Tree<T> { Leaf(T),",
            "  Node(Box<Tree<T>>, Box<Tree<T>>) }"
          ]
        }
      ]
