    {
      "page_title": "Tagged Union Layout & Niches",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Why It Beats C Unions",
          "text": "Enums replace the hand-rolled `tag + union` pattern, but the compiler owns the pairing — the tag can never disagree with the payload it describes."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Tagged Union Layout",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Enum value = discriminant + that variant's payload",
            "Rule of thumb: tag + largest variant",
            "Then round up to the alignment"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "array",
          "spec": {
            "cells": [
              "tag",
              "pad",
              "pad",
              "pad",
              "payload",
              "payload",
              "payload",
              "payload"
            ],
            "indices": true,
            "pointers": [],
            "highlight": [],
            "dim": [],
            "caption": "`enum E { A(u8), B(u64) }` = 16 bytes"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Not 9 bytes: `u64` aligns to 8, so the one-byte tag eats a whole 8-byte slot."
        },
