        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "What is `enum Never {}` good for?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Zero possible values, size 0, uninhabited",
            "`Result<T, Never>` is the same size as `T`",
            "Matching it needs no arms — code is unreachable"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "No Null In The Language",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "rust",
          "lines": [
            "enum Option<T> { None, Some(T) }",
            "// in the prelude: no import needed",
            "let n: Option<i32> = None;"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Absence lives in the type, not in the value",
            "Compiler forces the check before you touch it",
            "`Option<T>` and `T` are different types",
            "`Some(2) + 2` will not compile — map or unwrap"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Why is null the billion-dollar mistake?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Hoare's own word for it, from ALGOL W",
            "Null makes every reference secretly nullable",
            "`Option<T>` marks only the ones that are"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Ask Before You Take"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`is_some()` / `is_none()` for plain booleans",
            "`is_some_and(|x| x > 3)` fuses test and predicate",
            "`unwrap()` panics blankly on `None`",
            "`expect(\"cfg loaded first\")` names the invariant"
          ]
        },
