          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`..=` is inclusive; exclusive `..` stable since 1.80",
            "A guard is an extra boolean on top of a pattern",
            "`@` binds the value while still testing the pattern"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Guards Do Not Count",
          "text": "The exhaustiveness checker ignores guards. `Some(n) if n > 0` plus `Some(n) if n <= 0` still demands another arm — the compiler cannot prove arithmetic."
        },
